# Bureau Trivy Ignore File
# Suppress known false positives and accepted risks.
#
# Format: CVE-YYYY-NNNNN
# Always document WHY each entry is suppressed.

# ─── Node.js / npm ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example: CVE-2023-XXXXX — Affects only browser environments, not Node.js server
# CVE-2023-XXXXX

# ─── Development dependencies only ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Example: CVE affecting vitest/test runner — not in production build
# CVE-2024-XXXXX

# ─── Accepted risks with mitigations ─────────────────────────────────────────

# Example: prototype pollution in legacy dep — mitigated by input sanitization
# Add CVEs here with justification when accepted by security review

# ─── Policy ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every suppressed CVE must:
# 1. Have a documented reason
# 2. Have a review date (no older than 90 days)
# 3. Be approved by the security review process
#
# DO NOT suppress CRITICAL CVEs without security team sign-off.
